---
import LandingLayout from "../layouts/LandingLayout.astro";
import { landingLinks } from "../lib/landing-links";
---

<LandingLayout
  title="FAQ · Message Crate"
  description="Common questions about Message Crate."
  canonicalPath="/faq/"
>
  <main class="mv-stub mv-faq">
    <h1>FAQ</h1>
    <p>Short answers. The full story lives in the user guide.</p>

    <details open>
      <summary>What is Message Crate?</summary>
      <p>
        Software you run to extract messages from phone backups, store them on a
        machine you control, and browse, search, and export them yourself.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Is this a cloud product?</summary>
      <p>
        No. You run the server on a machine you control. Bitrealm does not host
        your message archive.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need my own backups?</summary>
      <p>
        Yes. Message Crate works from backups and exports you already have (for
        example iPhone backups, Android SMS tools, WhatsApp exports). See the
        user guide for supported sources.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Where do I start?</summary>
      <p>
        Read the
        <a href={landingLinks.docs}>user guide</a>
        or
        <a href={landingLinks.download}>download a release</a>
        from GitHub.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Where is the developer documentation?</summary>
      <p>
        See the
        <a href={landingLinks.developer}>developer documentation</a>
        for running from source, Docker, and internals.
      </p>
    </details>
  </main>
</LandingLayout>
